**.vscode/
**target/
**Cargo.lock
**/*.rs.bk
**.DS_Store
**.claude/

# Local design docs, plans and investigation reports. Never committed: the issue tracker is for
# defects and measurable optimisations, and docs/ is for everything else.
#
# Root-anchored on purpose — a leading "/" with no "**" prefix, unlike every pattern above. Those
# are meant to match at any depth (a build `target/` or a stray `.DS_Store` can turn up anywhere);
# this one must not, or a future `assets/docs/` of rendered example output would vanish from the
# index without a word. Verified with `git check-ignore -v`: bare `docs/` and `**docs/` both match
# at ANY depth, because git only anchors a pattern that has a leading or a middle slash and a
# trailing slash alone does not anchor anything. `/docs/` is the spelling that means "the top-level
# tree, and only that one". Aligned with smear's `.gitignore`, which carries the same finding.
/docs/

# Python bytecode from the CI helpers, which are run rather than imported.
**__pycache__/
